nyms, gene symbols) or unanchored heads describing a specific patient's presenting condition count as SpecificDisease, while unanchored heads in generic frames—syndrome feature lists, \"characterized by\" constructions, enumerated differentials—count as DiseaseClass. I'm adding negative constraints so modifiers alone don't convert labels, patient context doesn't override a generic clause frame, and category-level names for whole families of disorders stay DiseaseClass even when anchored. I'll finalize this as a single bulleted principle with IF/THEN logic and the negative constraints as sub-bullets, keeping the output strictly to that list.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Individuated-Referent Test for Disease Mentions:** IF a disease mention (a) contains a proper-name, eponym, acronym, gene-symbol, or enzyme-defined anchor in its head or immediate modifier, regardless of grammatical number, OR (b) is an unanchored head noun, with or without adjectival modifiers, that names the diagnosed or presenting condition of a specific individual in the text (e.g., a participial \"presenting with…\" phrase, a \"found to have…\" construction, or a clausal subject/predicate describing one patient), THEN label the head disease mention SpecificDisease. IF an unanchored head noun instead occurs in a generic frame, such as a syndrome-level list of characteristic features (\"characterized by…\"), or an enumerated differential introduced by a comparative construction (\"other causes of…\"), THEN label it DiseaseClass.\n  - **Negative constraint:** Do not promote an unanchored term to SpecificDisease solely because a patient appears elsewhere in the document; the clause frame containing the term governs. Do not treat plural number or added modifiers as evidence of a class label when an anchor is present. Modifiers alone never change the label, which is determined by the disease head noun. Anchored terms that name a broad grouping of distinct disorders rather than one disease entity remain DiseaseClass.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2345, "output_tokens": 3365, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2922}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}